  "name": "blog-discourse",
  "description": "Research what people are actually saying about a topic in the last 30 days across Reddit, X / Twitter, YouTube, Hacker News, dev.to, Medium, and other public discourse platforms. API-free; uses WebSearch with platform-targeted site operators plus recency filters. Produces DISCOURSE.md (a structured brief) and JSON output the writer can consume. Complements blog-researcher (which focuses on authority sources) with a recency-and-engagement lens. Not for verifying statistics (blog-factcheck) or gathering authority sources. Use when user says \"blog discourse\", \"discourse research\", \"what are people saying about\", \"research what people are saying\", \"voice of customer\", \"social listening\", \"30-day research\", \"trend research\", \"what's the discussion on\", \"real-time research\", \"practitioner discourse\", \"/blog discourse\".",
